From 8f2669a1f16bd850d51c7da19a6e7dea00c40af8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:57:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: test current hit points, not the item count, before
 banishing with the artifact

The Banishment defence may activate an artifact that banishes evil
monsters, but only with more than 100 hit points. The test read
borg.has[BI_CURHP], which counts how many of an unrelated object kind the
Borg carries (borg.has[] is indexed by object kind), so it was almost
never true and the artifact was never used. Test borg.trait[BI_CURHP].

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#37.

(cherry picked from commit caa6c6acc70c35ced4bfaaf2781036d99b5d32e5)
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
index 05e6ac00e..6945ec261 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-defend.c
@@ -2495,7 +2495,7 @@ static int borg_defend_aux_banishment(int p1)
         return 0;
 
     using_artifact
-        = borg_equips_item(act_loskill, true) && borg.has[BI_CURHP] > 100;
+        = borg_equips_item(act_loskill, true) && borg.trait[BI_CURHP] > 100;
 
     if (!using_artifact && !borg_spell_okay_fail(BANISH_EVIL, fail_allowed))
         return 0;
-- 
